---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="NO BALL GAMES Projects | Art, Games, Lore, Collectibles & Street Culture"
  description="Explore NO BALL GAMES projects across graffiti art, grime culture, digital collectibles, character lore, gaming concepts, clothing and community campaigns."
  current="projects"
>
  <section class="page-hero">
    <span class="eyebrow">Projects</span>
    <h1>A brand system with more than one lane.</h1>
    <p>
      NO BALL GAMES can expand across art, digital collectibles, gaming, clothing, events, community drops and story worlds. This page gives each lane a clear home.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="section project-grid">
    <article class="feature-card">
      <span class="kicker">01 • Art</span>
      <h3>Street art and grime art archive</h3>
      <p>Paintings, walls, sketches, jackets, characters, signs and raw visual work connected to the NO BALL GAMES identity.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="feature-card">
      <span class="kicker">02 • Collectibles</span>
      <h3>NFT and digital collectible structure</h3>
      <p>A future-ready area for character drops, collector passes, burn mechanics, rarity pages and on-chain culture without overloading the homepage.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="feature-card">
      <span class="kicker">03 • Gaming</span>
      <h3>Play against the rules</h3>
      <p>Mini-games, Telegram games, browser games, scoreboards, quests and community competitions can all sit under the same rebel-play concept.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="feature-card">
      <span class="kicker">04 • Clothing</span>
      <h3>Wearable street culture</h3>
      <p>Hand-painted jackets, denim, patches, prints, stencil pieces and future apparel drops can be presented as premium limited releases.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="feature-card">
      <span class="kicker">05 • Lore</span>
      <h3>Characters and world-building</h3>
      <p>The sign can become a mythology: characters, gangs, estates, courts, blocked zones, secret games and coded messages.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="feature-card">
      <span class="kicker">06 • Community</span>
      <h3>Fans, collectors and creators</h3>
      <p>Community challenges, artist callouts, collector spotlights, collabs and local culture can keep the brand active between major drops.</p>
    </article>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
